omponents, including scripts, renders, and assets, to prevent unintended modifications to the V5 pipeline.\n\n\nHalftones use **crosshatching** and **stepped shading**, achieving a non-photorealistic (NPR) material system. Instead of flat cartoon shadi\n<truncated 2364 bytes>\nncing smooth camera movements with stepped animation for secondary elements like the car and speed effects. A hybrid approach will be implemented where camera motion remains on ones at 24fps for smoothness, while car motion and graphic overlays step on twos at 12fps. Smooth motion blur should be disabled or significantly reduced to embrace the show's stylistic crispness and substitute it with graphical streak effects.\n\n\nThe *Across the Spider-Verse* reference suggests a structured visual rhythm across the 90-second lap. This rhythm can be split into three distinct visual dimensions for Silverstone's three sectors, each associated with a different Spider-Verse Earth: Brooklyn Classic Comic, Gwen Stacy Expressionist Watercolor, and Nueva York 2099 Cyberpunk Graphic. This division allows the incorporation of a variety of techniques within a single video. This approach provides a palette and artistic direction for applying stylized effects.\n\n\nThe goal is to integrate the distinct visual styles of *Across the Spider-Verse* across the Silverstone track sectors and implement a style selection feature for flexible visual control. Defining a configurable palette system via command-line options allows instant switching between visual styles.\n\nAn *audio remix* will blend the telemetry audio with specific *Spider-Verse* sonic signatures. The plan artifact (`spiderverse_v6_plan.md`) must adhere to strict artifact creation guidelines, especially those in `<artifacts>`. The plan will be saved with appropriate metadata for feedback and user accessibility, in a dedicated directory.\n\n\nThe project plan needs a `Details` section, a visual *Architecture* diagram, and a Swarm execution phase breakdown.  It should include Github-style alerts to emphasize key points, following the *<artifacts>* creation rule and `<communication_style>` guidelines.  I will focus on including clickable `file://` links to facilitate quick access to referenced files. The plan will also incorporate clear technical pipeline design and a performance budget.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["thinking"]}
