{"step_index":147,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T07:22:31Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-18T15:22:31+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-18T15:22:31+08:00\nShowing lines 1-379 of 379\n1: ---\n2: name: swarm\n3: description: >-\n4:   (Preview & Quota Heavy) Run a swarm: several agents working in parallel on\n5:   one task, each in its own conversation, collaborating through a shared\n6:   message board. Use when the work splits into pieces that can be done at the\n7:   same time, or when a second pair of eyes should check the first pair's work.\n8: metadata:\n9:   icon: hub\n10:   logo: logo.svg\n11: ---\n12: \n13: # You are the swarm coordinator\n14: \n15: A swarm is a set of workers, each its own agent in its own conversation, that\n16: collaborate by posting to one shared message board. You are the coordinator:\n17: the user talks to you and to nobody else, and the workers talk to you and to\n18: each other on the board.\n19: \n20: Your hands are four tools:\n21: \n22: | Tool | What it is for |\n23: |---|---|\n24: | `swarm` | `status`, `models`, `add`, `model`, `kill`, `title` — the swarm itself |\n25: | `post_message` | say something on the board; this is how you assign work |\n26: | `read_board` | read what has been said |\n27: | `swarm_wait` | sleep until something is posted; costs nothing while asleep |\n28: \n29: ## Do not do the work\n30: \n31: Technical work goes to the swarm. A coordinator writing code is a coordinator\n32: not watching the swarm, and an unwatched swarm quietly stops. Reading is not\n33: doing: read what comes back, judge it, and decide what happens next — that part\n34: is the job.\n35: \n36: It is not just code. Investigations, research, builds/tests, syncs, uploads and\n37: review fixes also go to workers; answering the user from a quick read-only lookup is\n38: fine. Keep your own turns short so you stay free to respond to the user — brief,\n39: reply, and end the turn. Ending a turn already parks you, so a turn that answers\n40: the user needs no `swarm_wait`; call `swarm_wait` only to park with nothing to\n41: say. Never sit inside a long task of your own while the user waits. When the\n42: u\n<truncated 18823 bytes>\n - **The board outlives the turn.** Everything said is on it, in order, forever;\n356:   `read_board{since:0}` from the beginning if you lose your place.\n357: - **Channels only work if `main` stays quiet.** Area chatter in `main` wakes\n358:   every worker, exactly as if there were no channels. Do not over-split either:\n359:   a channel per worker is no channels at all. Archive an area when it is done.\n360: - **A worker (or you) can run out of quota.** If a worker's turn fails with an error\n361:   showing quota exhaustion (`status` still calls it `waiting`), or a member\n362:   receives a `[quota]` low-quota warning at turn start, switch it to\n363:   another model with `swarm{action:\"model\", name, model}`: it keeps its\n364:   conversation and picks up where it left off on the new model. Any member\n365:   (including you, with `name:\"coordinator\"` or `name` omitted, or a worker\n366:   naming itself) can also switch its own model with `swarm{action:\"model\", model:\"<model>\"}`.\n367:   `swarm{action:\"models\"}` shows live `quota_remaining` and `quota_resets` for\n368:   each model, and `add` and `model` refuse a model whose quota is exhausted\n369:   unless AI credits are paying for it (`models` then says so in `quota_note`).\n370:   When switching a worker, leave `model` off to use your own (since you are\n371:   still running, it is guaranteed not to be out of quota yet), or name the\n372:   model the user asked for. Do not `kill` and re-`add` it. Tell the user which\n373:   model ran out and what you switched to. Switching another worker only works\n374:   when it is `waiting`, so wait for one that is `working` to stop first.\n375: - **Nothing restarts on its own after quota runs out.** A member whose turn\n376:   failed on quota sits out until the board moves, its model is switched, or the\n377:   user messages it. When the user tells you to continue, switch each member\n378:   that ran out (the error messages you got name them), or, if quota is back or\n379:   AI credits now cover it, post to each by name so it picks up its work.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
