izing rigorous QA after Iteration 2 is essential to avoid wasted render time.\n\nUser commands and skills indicate a specific request for indefinite iteration, leveraging all available resources. Reviewing available skills emphasizes the need for concise resp\n<truncated 173 bytes>\nwhen Iteration 1 is complete. Posting a roadmap that includes Art-Director feedback, upgrades, and a 2161-frame master render is essential.\n\n\nThe `@verifier` must now act as a strict art director and technical critic for Iteration 1, assessing various visual aspects. It should then send Iteration 2 polish items to specialized workers before tagging the coordinator for the final render. Reviewing the skills document reveals that workers should only mention the next peer and tag the coordinator only when the final deliverable is ready or there's a blocker.\n\n\nThe directive to iterate indefinitely suggests optimizing the swarm's resource use. Starting with a lean authoring swarm during development followed by spawning sharded render workers once Iteration 2 passes review aligns perfectly with the 'SKILL.md' guidance. This staged approach, keeping the swarm lean initially, mirrors the principle of adding workers only when genuine independent work queues, which is a key tenet of efficient swarm management.\n\n\nInitial plan involves sharding workers under a single role. The process involves passing tasks as slices with shared instructions or creating homogeneous copies to spawn workers in a single call.\n\nThe current stage necessitates a rigorous art-direction critique by the verifier of Iteration 1. This includes assessing distance-adaptive ink weight and the readability of halftone and hatching patterns at 1080p, specifically scrutinizing the output for clarity across various focal distances and visual elements.\n\n\nAssessing Iteration 1's output necessitates verifying specific visual qualities against *Across the Spider-Verse* to guide Iteration 2 improvements. This involves checking for visible halftone dots and crosshatching, distinct visual styles across the three universe acts, clear hero/background contrast with print-like misregistration, and confirming whether to add 3D comic effects. The verifier will directly drive one full polish cycle for Iteration 2 with specialized workers before coordinating final render.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"post_message","args":{"text":"\"@verifier **UPGRADED MANDATE — UNLIMITED ITERATION TO ULTIMATE MASTER EDITION**:\\nThe user granted unlimited resources to iterate all the way to the strongest possible final V6 Spider-Verse edition (including full 2,161-frame 1080p master film + V5-vs-V6 split-screen comparison at the end).\\n\\nTherefore, do NOT rubber-stamp Iteration 1! When `@sfx` hands Iteration 1 (`v6_stage_anim_sv.blend` + 26 stills + 3× 4s clips + audio) to you:\\n1) Run a **Ruthless Spider-Verse Art-Director + Quantitative Critique** across all 26 stills and all 3 clips:\\n   - **Ink Weight Across Scales**: Check close-ups (`S02`, `S09`) vs telephotos (`S13`, `S20`) — ensure `Solidify` + `Normal/Mist` ink outlines never blot thin wings/Halo into black clumps at distance and never vanish up close.\\n   - **1080p Halftone & Crosshatch Visibility**: Measure local frequency/contrast in midtone & shadow car/track bands to confirm Ben-Day dots and 45-deg pen crosshatching are unmistakably visible at 1080p (not washed out or sub-pixel).\\n   - **3-Act Universe Separation**: Confirm Act I (Earth-1610 graphic comic), Act II (Earth-65 Gwen Kuwahara watercolor wash), and Act III (Earth-928 2099 cyber neon + `f=1698..1699` Impact Frame) have dramatic, cinema-grade visual contrast and clean Hero-Car pop against CMYK-misregistered backgrounds.\\n   - **3D Comic FX Richness**: Identify high-impact Iteration-2 upgrades (e.g. 3D stepped exhaust afterburner/upshift burst cones, kerb-strike graphic spark slashes, sharper portal-cut comic panel tears, audio mix balance).\\n2) **Drive at least ONE full Iteration-2 Polish cycle** directly by posting concrete, shot-specific art-direction & shader/compositor/SFX upgrades to `@env-2` -> `@anim` -> `@sfx`!\\n3) Once Iteration 2 (or 3) passes 10/10 cinema-grade QA on all 26 stills & 3 clips, tag `@coordinator` with `READY_FOR_FULL_MASTER_RENDER` + per-frame CPU speed so `@coordinator` spawns a sharded parallel Blender render pool for all 2,161 frames + the final master & V5-vs-V6 split-screen films!\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking"]}
