{"step_index":161,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T07:38:30Z","input_tokens":3131,"cache_read_tokens":263547,"output_tokens":3378,"thinking":"The timing suggests reusable Spider-Verse assets are already built in `env-2` and `anim` environments. Shader, texture, and compositor nodes from those builds could be leveraged. The presence of these files indicates potential for significant optimization.\n\n\nThe existing assets offer a foundation for a new 3D circuit (\"V7 / V6-Ultra\"). The user's feedback (\"not satisfied with the circuit design,\" \"not enough sense of the lens,\" \"rendering effects are not good,\" \"more impact\") necessitates a redesign with enhanced cinematography and a high-impact render system. A new worker dedicated to the 3D circuit generator is needed to pursue this. The architecture must be non-colliding, split into 4 pieces.\n\n\nThe existing V6 architecture can be cleanly upgraded by redesigning it as a \"V6 Spider-Verse Mega-Circuit\". A new `track` engineer is needed because `env-2` and `anim` are completing their turns and the circuit design requires computation of 3D elevation, banked turns, and other dynamic properties. The goal is a shorter, denser, and more action-packed circuit, leveraging Spider-Verse assets for maximum visual impact.\n\n\nThe initial 5.8 km lap's object density was too low, resulting in large empty spaces between assets. Reducing the circuit to approximately 3.4–3.8 km allows for a significant increase in architectural and prop density, potentially tripling the objects per meter. This tighter design will necessitate continuous set-pieces every six seconds, eliminating flat, uninteresting sections.\n\n\nInitial design concepts incorporate intense visuals: a steep uphill S-crest, a suspended sky-bridge above a neon harbor, and a Laguna-Seca-style